Q1: Why Matrix Product State (MPS)?

Quantum simulators in Qiskit offer multiple simulation methods, each with critical trade-offs:

1. standard statevector: simulating N qubits requires 2^N complex amplitudes in RAM. Beyond ~30 qubits, standard machines run out of memory. 
For two qubits, the state has four amplitudes:
|ψ> = a00|00> + a01|01> + a10|10> + a11|11>

2. stabilizer: Cannot simulate CNOT / non-Clifford gates

3. MPS: MPS simulates 100+ QKD qubits in linear time O(N) with negligible memory overhead.

Q2: Why seed?

Basically an initialiser for random number generator, if we dont provide seed, we will get different result for same code, if we provide seed, we will get same result for same code.




